Original commit body from f36269f911b7aa6005272c290a96dcdecce88d23:

INV-titih. `_validate_catalog_dict` accepted `status: complete` on four
conditions — the literal string, a present stdlib_provenance.source_url,
an https scheme, an allowlisted hostname — and counted no rows.
python.yaml carried `complete` from 2026-05-14 while holding no row for
os.open or os.write, the exact pair INV-zubuh measured producing a
"never writes to the host filesystem" confirm. The WORD asserted
coverage; the CHECK asserted a citation. Surfaced by the owner asking,
reasonably: "isn't os part of stdlib? i thought we completed the stdlib
catalog."

RESOLUTION: rename, not a coverage gate. The coverage claim already has
exactly one checked home — module_completeness, the dated per-module
audit mechanism (per-slot, exact-match) — so teaching `status` to count
rows would put one fact in two homes. The item's three senses of
"complete" become one word each:

  provenance_declared   the citation check (this rename)
  module_completeness   the dated per-module coverage audit
  "complete" (plain English)   REFUSED at load, with an error naming
                               INV-titih and pointing at both homes

The refusal is the class fix the item demands ("do NOT simply add the
six os rows and leave the label"): the overclaiming spelling cannot
silently return, and the validator never acquires a row-counting duty
its value does not name.

Mechanics:
- Vocabulary {provenance_declared, in_progress}; the four citation
  checks unchanged under the new name (pinned by
  test_io_boundary_status_provenance_declared.py).
- 3 shipped catalogues carried the live label (python, rust, erlang);
  renamed. The 11 in_progress catalogues' "promotion to ``status:
  complete``" comments rewritten — promotion requires the citation
  only, coverage is claimed per-module.
- _from_dict's absent-status default follows the rename (a status-less
  catalogue required provenance before and still does — equivalent
  behavior).
- Overlay refusal message, dataclass docstring, in_progress_languages
  docstring, MIGRATION-IO-BOUNDARIES.md updated.
- Behavior-neutral for consumers: production branches only on
  `status == "in_progress"` (two sites), never on the renamed value.

Split out, not folded in: load_catalog returns the dataclass default
for a MISSING catalogue file, so uncatalogued languages read as
provenance_declared. Changing that flips dst_classification_unreliable
for catalogue-less languages — behavioral, needs its own measurement;
pinned as-is by test_missing_catalog_default_pinned_as_is and filed as
a work item.

